# Text that ships or gets committed keeps LF everywhere. The CSVs matter most:
# tools/hash-strings.ps1 and the in-game "Hash for commit" both run on Windows,
# and without a rule here the result depends on the contributor's core.autocrlf.
# A CRLF that lands inside a quoted multi-line translation becomes part of the
# translated string, because CsvReader keeps every character inside quotes.
*.sh  text eol=lf
*.csv text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf

# Belt and braces. Git already detects these as binary from their NUL bytes,
# but an explicit rule keeps that true if a `* text=auto` line is ever added.
*.bundle binary
*.gif    binary
